+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_add_of_exact", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem finrank_add_of_exact {k A B C : Type*} [Field k] [AddCommGroup A] [Module k A] [AddCommGroup B] [Module k B] [AddCommGroup C] [Module k C] [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Finite k C] (f : A \u2192\u2097[k] B) (g : B \u2192\u2097[k] C) (hf : Function.Injective f) (hg : Function.Surjective g) (hfg : Function.Exact f g) : finrank k B = finrank k A + finrank k C", "doc": "**Additivity of `finrank` along a short exact sequence.** For a short exact sequence of finite-dimensional `k`-vector spaces `0 \u2192 A \u2192f B \u2192g C \u2192 0` (`f` injective, `g` surjective, `Function.Exact f g`), the dimension of the middle term is the sum of the outer dimensions: `finrank k B = finrank k A + finrank k C`.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 69}
