+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_quotSucc_jump", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem finrank_quotSucc_jump {I : Ideal B} (h : I.IsPrincipal) (h' : I \u2260 \u22a5) (n : \u2115) [Module.Finite k (B \u29f8 I)] : finrank k ((I ^ n : Ideal B) \u29f8 (I \u2022 \u22a4 : Submodule B (I ^ n : Ideal B))) = finrank k (B \u29f8 I)", "doc": "**One-step filtration jump.**  For a nonzero principal ideal `I = (\u03c0)`, multiplication by `\u03c0 ^ n` induces a `B`-linear (hence `k`-linear) isomorphism `B \u29f8 I \u2243 I ^ n \u29f8 I \u2022 \u22a4`, so the two quotients have the same `k`-dimension.     * Provenance: CUSTOM.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Algebra/DedekindColength.lean", "line": 135}
